(1) Calculate the energy conversion efficiency of the lactic acid fermentation process (keep two significant figures);
(2) If 1 mol of glucose releases a total of 2870 kJ of energy during aerobic respiration with an energy conversion efficiency of approximately 40%, calculate the difference in energy dissipated as heat (kJ) between 1 mol of glucose undergoing anaerobic respiration (lactic acid fermentation) and aerobic respiration.

