2. Biological Significance:
① Reflecting pigment types: The four color bands in the model reflect that green leaves contain four major types of photosynthetic pigments;
② Reflecting pigment content: The width of the bands reflects the differences in the content of various pigments in the leaves (chlorophyll a is the widest, indicating the highest content);
③ Reflecting functional differences: Combined with the absorption spectrum model, pigments at different positions correspond to different light absorption characteristics, which together constitute the physiological basis for the efficient utilization of visible light by plants.

