【Problem Statement】Given 21 types of amino acids and the condition that each amino acid does not repeat within the peptide chain, how many possible permutations are there for a short peptide composed of 12 amino acids?

【Calculation Process】
1. This is a permutation problem. There are 21 choices of amino acids for the first position;
2. Since each amino acid appears at most once, there are 20 choices remaining for the second position, 19 for the third, and so on;
3. There are (21 - 12 + 1) = 10 choices for the 12th position;
4. According to the multiplication principle, the total number = 21 × 20 × 19 × 18 × 17 × 16 × 15 × 14 × 13 × 12 × 11 × 10.
Or using the permutation formula: A(21, 12) = 21! / (21-12)!

【Final Result】
The theoretical number of short peptide types that can be synthesized is: 21! / 9! = 21 × 20 × 19 × 18 × 17 × 16 × 15 × 14 × 13 × 12 × 11 × 10 = 12,015,316,051,200 (or expressed as A(21, 12)).

