questions.question_en:
A research group plans to artificially synthesize a protein consisting of 3 peptide chains. It is known that the average relative molecular mass of the amino acids composing this protein is 128. It has been determined that a total of 100 water molecules were removed during the synthesis of this protein. Please design a scheme to calculate the relative molecular mass of this protein and write down the specific calculation steps:
1. Based on the number of water molecules removed, calculate the total number of amino acids composing the protein;
2. Calculate the total relative molecular mass of all amino acids;
3. Calculate the total mass of the removed water molecules;
4. Finally, derive the relative molecular mass of the protein.

