In the experiment observing the plasmolysis and deplasmolysis of the outer epidermal cells of purple onion scale leaves, a student observed and measured the state of the same cell at equilibrium in different concentrations of sucrose solution through a microscope. It is known that the cell undergoes plasmolysis in a 0.3 g/mL sucrose solution. At this time, the long axis length of the cell (cell wall length) was measured as L, and the long axis length of the protoplast (protoplast layer and internal substances) was measured as W. If L = 100 μm for this cell, and W = 75 μm when equilibrium is reached in the 0.3 g/mL sucrose solution; subsequently, the cell is placed in pure water and observed to undergo full recovery, at which point W' = 98 μm. Please calculate:

(1) The "degree of plasmolysis" (expressed as W/L, keep two decimal places) when the cell undergoes plasmolysis in the 0.3 g/mL sucrose solution;
(2) During the process from the state of plasmolysis to full recovery, how many μm did the protoplast length increase?

