A biology interest group intends to verify through experiments that "ATP is the direct energy source for muscle contraction." It is known that under experimental conditions, for every 1 mmol of ATP consumed by isolated muscle tissue, the energy released can cause the muscle to produce a contractile force of 0.05 N (this ratio is independent of muscle mass). Three identical groups of isolated muscle tissue were prepared and treated as follows:
Group A: Add a certain concentration of glucose solution;
Group B: Add an equal volume of ATP solution;
Group C: First add a respiratory inhibitor (to block endogenous ATP production); after the muscle stops contracting, add the same amount of ATP solution as in Group B.
(1) Please complete the experimental steps and predict the experimental results to verify the conclusion.
(2) If the muscle in Group C produced a contractile force of 0.2 N in the experiment, please calculate the minimum amount of ATP (in mmol) consumed by the muscle in Group C after the addition of ATP.
